      "side": 0,
      "message": "I imagine baseboard as 1) a library of components that variant boards can select from and 2) a place where all \"very\" common defines can go.\n\nTo achieve #1, I need to define items in board.h before baseboard.h is included, but there is a ordering problem that baseboard\u0027s defines (e.g. EC chip defines) need to be before \"register.h\" in board.h.\n\nI am also overriding a baseboard-common define in yorp/board.h [0]: USB_A port count (since yorp\u0027s reason to set to 1 instead of 2 was a hardware issue that is fixing going forward). That is the paradigm I envision us using.\n\n[0] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1038898/3/board/yorp/board.h#26",
